"ac427db613f73d0a4187900dd23e9c5c5a72bff5": {"body":"As of 15:04 UTC: Lisbon's red rain ended at 15:00 as IPMA's 12:33 messages set it (s-1111T1503);\nyellow rain and orange wind to 18:00, orange sea to 21:00; red rain in Santarem and Faro to\n18:00. Observed: 74 km/h gust at the airport at 14:00 (our record's highest), 26.2 mm at Oeiras\nin hour 13:00 (heaviest hour at IPMA's Lisbon stations in our record) (s-1111T1425); the\nmeteorologist's analysis 21 (centre just north) as hypothesis; ANA's own figures (fact),\nTranstejo's vehicle stop (fact), the Interior Ministry's end of the alert (evidence). Warnings\ndrawn from IPMA's open data again (no CAP overrides). Editions 1-6 unchanged.","session":"session_018yvwtPVWJtSb1BoAg7xMvW","files":[{"p":"brief/README.md","a":6,"d":5},{"p":"brief/edition-7.json","a":346,"d":0},{"p":"brief/edition-7.md","a":21,"d":0},{"p":"tools/brief-make.mjs","a":2,"d":2}],"more_files":0},
